Falsifies `file_allocation_table::write_cursor::verification::a_write_extends_the_chain_to_the_size_and_stays_inside_it`.

The defect: a write that ends before the file does shrinks the size to where it stopped, so overwriting the head of a file loses the bytes after it from every reader that trusts the entry.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(state.size as usize, size)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/write_cursor.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/write_cursor.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/write_cursor.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/write_cursor.rs
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ impl WriteState {
             }
             self.position += len as u32;
             done += len;
-            self.size = self.size.max(self.position);
+            self.size = self.position;
         }
         Ok(done)
     }
